# Settings for setup.sh. Copy to setup.conf next to setup.sh.

# Everything (runner, Bulava, claude, codex, tmux, git, the project's Docker stack) runs as the user
# who owns this folder and runs `sudo ./setup.sh` from it; there is nothing to set. Setup creates no
# users and changes nobody's sudo. The isolation boundary is the VM: the workers run as this user
# and can read the runner's tokens.

# Pinned tool versions. Change them here, re-run setup: the old version is replaced.
CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=2.1.295
CODEX_VERSION=0.162.0
CHROME_DEVTOOLS_MCP_VERSION=1.10.1   # the version Bulava's automation-mcp.json pins

# Bulava engine (engine/SERVER.md): the public repository, installed to /opt/bulava.
#   BULAVA_SOURCE  a git URL, or a directory here. Empty BULAVA_SOURCE skips the engine phases.
#   BULAVA_REF     a full commit to stay on (the default), a tag, or a branch the server follows.
#                  setup refuses to swap the engine while a task is running: run it between tasks.
# A full commit, because Bulava rewrites its branches: `factory` and `main` were squashed into one
# commit, and the SHAs the server ran before stopped existing upstream. Every commit setup installs
# is kept in /var/lib/arceus/bulava.git, so the server can be rebuilt on it whatever happens upstream.
# To update: put the new commit here (`git ls-remote <source> refs/heads/main`), check its
# engine/SERVER.md, and run `sudo ./setup.sh` between tasks. `factory` is where Bulava puts server
# fixes first; BULAVA_REF=factory follows it, taking its newest commit on every run.
# b721e5f (2026-10-26): the independent Claude checks before Codex (bulava.claude_checks in config.yaml).
# 93746a0 (2026-10-27, main, 1.16.3): b721e5f plus fixes: Codex reviews Cyrillic tasks, the write-gate's
# false refusals, `codex` on the task says where Codex did not take part.
BULAVA_SOURCE=https://github.com/Stepanokdev/bulava
BULAVA_REF=93746a05a5336702c785e64f0928dc40747d73e4
